 hand significantly. It is much better to keep the straight intact and look for an opportunity to play it or use the Ace later if the straight becomes unviable.\n\nReason: Teammate\'s K is strong enough to pressure the Landlord. Passing preserves my 10-J-Q-K-A straight and allows me to use my 2s to counter the Landlord if they play an Ace.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
